# Conformance probe pack for a switch key that does not read back (spec 0.20,
# ruling 31), most significant bit first. Public.
#
#   label : 8 uint via tbl (1 alpha, 256 big), then by label
#     big    x : 8
#     alpha  y : 8
#     else   z : 8
#
# big writes the low 8 bits of 256, 0; 0 has no table entry, so decode of
# those bits fails: the key does not read back and encode is
# transform-encode, because the output would not decode.
format     conformance-kinds-readback
version    0.20.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
map    tbl  1    alpha
map    tbl  256  big
field  probe.label  8  uint  via tbl
switch probe.label
  case big
    field  probe.x  8  uint
  case alpha
    field  probe.y  8  uint
  else
    field  probe.z  8  uint
end
